# Node.js / TypeScript

When editing matching files:

- Apply engineering foundations first (always-applied rule).
- Load `.cursor/skills/code/languages/nodejs/SKILL.md` for language rules.
- Load its `references/` only when the skill directs.
- Follow the nearest `AGENT.md` chain for project lint/build commands and type-alias conventions.

Key rules: no `any`, no `@ts-nocheck`, async/await only, no empty bound catch, only `console.error/warn`, prefer canonical/`@types/*` types over workarounds.
